{
  "version": "1.0",
  "name": "Quantum 1: Superposition and Collapse",
  "description": "The Quantum Microtubule - Penrose-Hameroff Orch-OR Theory\n\nBACKGROUND:\nRoger Penrose and Stuart Hameroff proposed that consciousness arises from \nquantum computations in microtubules - protein structures inside neurons.\n\nKEY CONCEPTS DEMONSTRATED:\n\n1. SUPERPOSITION\n   The quantum state exists in multiple configurations simultaneously.\n   Watch the 'probabilities' output - it shows the quantum probability \n   distribution across possible states.\n\n2. OBJECTIVE REDUCTION (COLLAPSE)\n   When the collapse_threshold is reached, the superposition collapses \n   to a single definite state. Penrose theorizes this collapse is \n   caused by quantum gravity effects.\n   \n3. COHERENCE\n   Quantum effects persist only while the system maintains coherence.\n   The coherence_time parameter controls how long quantum states survive\n   before decoherence (environmental interference).\n\nEXPERIMENT:\n- Adjust the input value and watch how it affects the quantum state\n- Lower collapse_threshold = more frequent collapses (more \"conscious moments\")\n- Higher noise_scale = faster decoherence\n\nRECENT RESEARCH (2022-2024):\nAnirban Bandyopadhyay's lab found quantum vibrations in microtubules at \nbody temperature - a key prediction of Orch-OR that skeptics thought \nimpossible. The debate continues!",
